# netsurf: custom element constructors, document.firstElementChild,
# PerformanceObserver entry lists (patch 240)
# Generated 2026-10-11
# Base: seleron/vitabrowser (patch stack through 239)
#
# github.com's last three JS errors, each Chromium-checked:
#
#  - Custom elements (vita_polyfill.js): the polyfill only swapped an
#    upgraded element's prototype, so a class constructor never ran --
#    Turbo's Object.getPrototypeOf(createElement("turbo-frame").delegate)
#    threw. HTMLElement is now a constructor that, while an element is
#    being upgraded, hands super() that element (the usual polyfill
#    technique), so constructors run for createElement(), `new` and
#    upgrades of parsed / inserted elements; connectedCallback and
#    disconnectedCallback run once per insertion / removal;
#    attributeChangedCallback for observedAttributes (that observer is
#    only created once a definition asks for it). The bridge reinstalls
#    document.createElement after the polyfill's first run (it runs twice
#    per context), so createElement is re-wrapped on every run, once per
#    native function.
#  - The document is a ParentNode: firstElementChild, lastElementChild,
#    childElementCount, children (undefined; "cannot read property
#    'classList' of undefined" on document.firstElementChild.classList).
#  - PerformanceObserver (still a no-op) calls back with an entry list
#    (getEntries / getEntriesByType / getEntriesByName), not a bare array
#    ("not a function" on e.getEntries()).
#
# Gates: testpages/pages/JS-custom-elements.html CUSTOMEL 7/7 (Chromium
# 7/7; before 2/7), JS-perfobserver.html PERFOBS 2/2 (Chromium 2/2;
# disarmed 1/2). github.com with 238-240: JS errors 9 -> 0.
#
